            <chunk name="Object" index="17">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">ce75dae5-dcf7-5f4d-9852-1725bf7b7dfa</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">README</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">DIAGRID ON A FREEFORM SURFACE

Divides any surface into a grid of bays and draws the two diagonals of every bay along the surface, producing a diagrid structure or facade pattern that follows the curvature.

HOW TO USE
1. Right-click 'Srf' and Set one Surface to use your own facade or roof surface (a sample is stored).
2. 'Bays U' and 'Bays V' set how many diamonds you get in each direction.
3. Leave the four corner MD Sliders as they are for a classic diagrid; moving them bends the diagonals inside each bay.
4. Bake the two Curve On Surface components to get the diagonals.

YOU WILL LEARN
- Divide Domain2 + Isotrim: splitting a surface into sub-surfaces
- Deconstruct Brep: faces, edges and vertices of a bay
- Curve On Surface: a curve defined by UV points that stays on the surface
- MD Slider: a 2D (UV) input

READ THE CANVAS LEFT TO RIGHT
Green = inputs you change, coloured boxes = numbered steps, blue = results.

SOURCE
Lucas Becker (runxel) - runxel/grasshopper-examples
gh/diagrid_on_surface.ghx @ 0e57586bdc
Licence: BlueOak-1.0.0 (see LICENCE panel)
Modified for the Almond parametric library: regrouped, relabelled and annotated; the geometric logic is unchanged.</item>
